ms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Introducing a singular term to be taken generically: preceding a name of something standing for a whole class.","example":"Stern and God-fearing, the Afrikaner takes his religion seriously.","frame_run_id":9,"frame_seq":8,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176335,"id":"the|determiner|9","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used with the plural of a surname to indicate the entire family.","example":"The Bushes have held political office for several decades and the Kennedys longer.","frame_run_id":9,"frame_seq":8,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176335,"id":"the|determiner|10","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Added to a superlative or an ordinal number to make it into a substantive.","example":"That apple pie was the best.","frame_run_id":9,"frame_seq":8,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176335,"id":"the|determiner|11","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before an adjective, indicating all things (especially persons) described by that adjective.","example":"Feed the hungry, clothe the naked, comfort the afflicted, and afflict the comfortable.","frame_run_id":9,"frame_seq":8,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176335,"id":"the|determiner|12","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before a demonym ending in 