:[],"token_index":3,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Added to a superlative or an ordinal number to make it into a substantive.","example":"That apple pie was the best.","frame_run_id":13,"frame_seq":12,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176658,"id":"the|determiner|11","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":3,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before an adjective, indicating all things (especially persons) described by that adjective.","example":"Feed the hungry, clothe the naked, comfort the afflicted, and afflict the comfortable.","frame_run_id":13,"frame_seq":12,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176658,"id":"the|determiner|12","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":3,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before a demonym ending in -ish or -ese to refer to people of a given country collectively.","example":"the Irish are...; the Chinese are...; the French are...","frame_run_id":13,"frame_seq":12,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176658,"id":"the|determiner|13","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":3,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative or with more and a verb phrase, establishes a correlation with one or more other such comparatives.","example":"The hotter(,) the better. (comma usually omitted in such very short expressions)","frame_run_id":13,"frame_seq":12,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176658,"id":"the|adverb|1","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":3,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative