ediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used to indicate a certain example of (a noun) which is usually of most concern or most common or familiar.","example":"No one in the whole country had seen it before.","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|3","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used before a body part, a family member, a pet (especially of someone previously mentioned), as an alternative to a possessive pronoun.","example":"A stone hit him on the head. (= “A stone hit him on his head.”)","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|4","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"active_cells","synonyms":[]},{"activation":0.25,"antonyms":[],"definition":"(colloquial) Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Precedes a familiar nickname or other term of address.","example":"How's the Sal today?","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"gram_function":[],"id":"the|determiner|5","lemma":"the","mw":false,"norm":"the","pos":"determiner","rel_prior":0.2,"score":0.5,"semantic_atom