leaſing, and diſagreeable circumſtances of life, thou endowedſt me with an equal, conſtant, manly, and ſuperior ſpirit on every occaſion.","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|pronoun|1","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"pronoun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:alt-of","tag:nonstandard","pos_raw:pron"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"a word-initial letter ⟨i⟩","example":null,"frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|phrase|2","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"phrase","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:3","pos_raw:symbol"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"the long vowel /aɪ/ at the end of a word, or before a final consonant that is not /dʒ, v, z/. (Note: the final consonant is not written.)","example":null,"frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|phrase|3","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"phrase","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:3","pos_raw:symbol"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"the words if, is, it, its","example":null,"frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|phrase|4","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"phrase","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:3","pos_raw:symbol"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(first-person, personal, pronoun, singular, subjective) The speaker or writer, referred to as the grammatical subject, of a sentence.","example":"[…]It ill beſeemes a knight of gentle ſort, / Such as ye haue him boaſted, to beguyle / A ſimple maide, and worke ſo hainous tort, / In ſhame of knighthood, as I largely can report.","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|pronoun|2","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"pronoun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:first-person","tag:personal","tag:pronoun","tag:singular","tag:subjective","pos_raw:pron"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(first-person, nonstandard, personal, pronoun, singular, subjective) The speaker or writer, referred to as the grammatical object, of a sentence.","example":"Mom drove my sister and I to school.","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|pronoun|3","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"pronoun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:first-person","tag:nonstandard","tag:personal","tag:pronoun","tag:singular","tag:subjective","pos_raw:pron"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(metaphysics, countable, uncountable) The ego.","example":"They are called men, becauſe each of them poſſeſſeth the whole man, though not wholly. There are by their means two I’s in every believer, Rom. vii. 15. For that which I do, I allow not: for what I would, that do I not; but what I hate, that do I. There is not one part of the man that is in Chriſt, but grace has a part of it, and corruption has a part of it: as in the twilight there is light over all, and darkneſs over all too, the darkneſs being mixed in every part with the light. So my renewed part is I, a man having an underſtanding enlightened, a will renewed, affections ſpiritualized, uſing my body conform: but my unrenewed part is I too, having an underſtanding darkened, a will rebellious, affections corrupted, and uſing my body accordingly.","frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|noun|2","lemma":"i","norm":"i","pos":"noun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:countable","tag:uncountable","qual:metaphysics","pos_raw:noun"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":["me#Noun"],"token_index":0,"word":"i"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(letter, uppercase) The ninth letter of the English alphabet, called i and written in the Latin script.","example":null,"frame_run_id":16,"frame_seq":15,"frame_ts_ms":1792296176936,"id":"i|phrase|5","le