ample":"Feed the hungry, clothe the naked, comfort the afflicted, and afflict the comfortable.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792298498118,"id":"the|determiner|12","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before a demonym ending in -ish or -ese to refer to people of a given country collectively.","example":"the Irish are...; the Chinese are...; the French are...","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792298498118,"id":"the|determiner|13","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative or with more and a verb phrase, establishes a correlation with one or more other such comparatives.","example":"The hotter(,) the better. (comma usually omitted in such very short expressions)","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792298498118,"id":"the|adverb|1","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative, and often with for it, indicates a result more like said comparative. This can be negated with none.","example":"It was a difficult time, but I’m the wiser for it.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792298498118,"id":"the|adverb|2","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) Beyond all others.","example":"We went the furthest under her leadership.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792298498118,"id":"the|adve