fore a noun designating something considered to be unique, or of which there is only one at a time.","example":"No one knows how many galaxies there are in the universe.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|2","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used to indicate a certain example of (a noun) which is usually of most concern or most common or familiar.","example":"No one in the whole country had seen it before.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|3","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used before a body part, a family member, a pet (especially of someone previously mentioned), as an alternative to a possessive pronoun.","example":"A stone hit him on the head. (= “A stone hit him on his head.”)","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|4","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(colloquial) Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Precedes a familiar nickname or other term of address.","example":"How's the Sal today?","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|5","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","tag:colloquial","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — The definite grammatical article that shows that the noun phrase that immediately follows it is definitely identifiable... — ...because it is presumed to be definitely known in context or from shared knowledge. — Used in many idiomatic expressions and proverbs to refer to common objects, roles, or situations connected with something definite, in the manner of an analogy","example":"square the circle; feel the pinch; beat around the bush; throw the baby out with the bathwater","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|6","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — When stressed, indicates that it describes something which is considered to be best or exclusively worthy of attention.","example":"That is the hospital to go to for heart surgery.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|7","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used before a noun phrase beginning with superlative or comparative adjective or an ordinal number, indicating that the noun refers to a single item.","example":"That was the juiciest apple pie ever.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|8","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Introducing a singular term to be taken generically: preceding a name of something standing for a whole class.","example":"Stern and God-fearing, the Afrikaner takes his religion seriously.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|9","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used before a noun phrase, including a simple noun — Used with the plural of a surname to indicate the entire family.","example":"The Bushes have held political office for several decades and the Kennedys longer.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|10","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Added to a superlative or an ordinal number to make it into a substantive.","example":"That apple pie was the best.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|11","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before an adjective, indicating all things (especially persons) described by that adjective.","example":"Feed the hungry, clothe the naked, comfort the afflicted, and afflict the comfortable.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|12","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"Used with an adjective — Used before a demonym ending in -ish or -ese to refer to people of a given country collectively.","example":"the Irish are...; the Chinese are...; the French are...","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|determiner|13","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:1","pos_raw:article"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative or with more and a verb phrase, establishes a correlation with one or more other such comparatives.","example":"The hotter(,) the better. (comma usually omitted in such very short expressions)","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|adverb|1","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) With a comparative, and often with for it, indicates a result more like said comparative. This can be negated with none.","example":"It was a difficult time, but I’m the wiser for it.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|adverb|2","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(not-comparable) Beyond all others.","example":"We went the furthest under her leadership.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|adverb|3","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"adverb","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:2","tag:not-comparable","rtag:with a superlative adjective","pos_raw:adv"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"For each; per.","example":"valued at half a pound the bushel; paying seven dollars the year interest","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|preposition|1","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"preposition","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:3","pos_raw:prep"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(alt-of, obsolete) Obsolete form of thee.","example":"Feſtus ſayde with a lowde voyce: Paul / thou arte beſides thy ſilfe. Moche learnynge hath made the mad.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"the|pronoun|1","lemma":"the","norm":"the","pos":"pronoun","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["ety:4","tag:alt-of","tag:obsolete","pos_raw:pron"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":2,"word":"the"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(interrogative) Which, especially which of an open-ended set of possibilities.","example":"What colour are you going to use?","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"what|determiner|1","lemma":"what","norm":"what","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["tag:interrogative","pos_raw:det"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"what"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(indirect, interrogative) Which.","example":"I wonder what colour he is going to use.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"id":"what|determiner|2","lemma":"what","norm":"what","pos":"determiner","score":0.5,"semantic_atoms":["tag:indirect","tag:interrogative","pos_raw:det"],"source":"ltm","synonyms":[],"token_index":0,"word":"what"},{"antonyms":[],"definition":"(relative) Any ... that; all ... that; whatever.","example":"He seems to have lost what sense he had.","frame_run_id":6,"frame_seq":5,"frame_ts_ms":1792300167359,"i